  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Seven Oaks is Nashville's most beloved course — exquisitely maintained, beautiful, and always busy, with 21 holes that swing from wide open to dense woods. The standard loop plays 5,737 feet at par 64, including three bonus holes that locals treat as a warm-down after the main 18.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and DISCatcher baskets on varied terrain that keeps every hole distinct. The course has been a fixture since 1989 and it shows — the fairways are groomed, the signs are clear, and the regulars are friendly.",
    "Come early to beat the crowd; on a nice afternoon this is the busiest course in town for good reason."
