  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 21 is Seven Oaks' bonus-loop finisher — 260 feet of well-groomed fairway that captures everything the course does well: clean lines, fair distance, and immaculate maintenance. It's the hole that keeps you playing just one more round after the main 18 is done.",
  "localTips": "The busiest course in Nashville — go early on weekends. The three bonus holes are numbered I–III on the course signs; they're the perfect warm-down. Free to play, varied terrain from open to dense woods, and the regulars are famously friendly.",
